## Example: multi-level menu

```python
from sumtui import Menu, MenuBar, MenuItem, Separator;

view_menu = Menu("View", [
    MenuItem("Text", view_text),
    MenuItem("Hex + ASCII", view_hex),
]);

bar = MenuBar([
    Menu("File", [
        MenuItem("Open", open_file),
        Separator(),
        MenuItem("Quit", quit_app, "F10"),
    ]),
    Menu("Command", [
        MenuItem("View mode", submenu=view_menu),
    ]),
]);
```

## Example: lazy hexadecimal viewer

```python
from sumtui import HexView;

viewer = HexView.from_file("large-image.raw", bytes_per_row=16);
```

Only the visible window is read on demand.

## Easy API

The easy layer remains available:

```python
import sumtui.easy as st;

st.screen("Example", theme="RAR");
status = st.statusbar("READY.");
files = st.table(["Name", "Size"]);
st.root(st.vbox(st.panel(files, title="Files"), status, sizes=[None, 1]));
st.start();
```

0.3 adds easy helpers for `groupbox`, `listview`, `tree`, `scrollbar`, `radiobutton`, `markdownview`, `syntaxview`, `hexview`, `menubar`, `contextmenu`, `splitter`, `filedialog`, and `directorydialog`.

## Syntax-aware viewer

```python
from sumtui import SyntaxView;

viewer = SyntaxView.from_file("README.md", syntax_theme="vim");
```

Long source lines remain available through Left/Right horizontal scrolling instead of being permanently clipped. Shift+Left/Right scrolls roughly one viewport; Ctrl+Left/Right jumps to the horizontal edge.

The lexer is inferred from the filename when possible. The RAR-style browser demo uses the same mechanism automatically and falls back to `HexView` for binary files.

## `sumprogress` pipe helper

`ProgressBar` remains a display widget. The package also installs a small command-line helper that makes the same idea useful in shell pipelines.

Feed percentages:

```bash
printf '10\n35\n80\n100\n' | sumprogress --percent-input --label Job
```

Or use it as a simple `pv`-style byte pass-through. Progress is written to stderr; the byte stream stays on stdout:

```bash
cat image.iso | sumprogress --total 4.7G --label Copy > image-copy.iso
```

Size suffixes `K`, `M`, `G`, and `T` use powers of 1024.

## Development demos use local source

Examples insert the project `src/` directory before importing `sumtui`. This prevents a globally/user-installed older release from masking changes while testing a source checkout.

## Self-test

```bash
sumtui --self-test
```

